{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-point-of-sale-android-terminals-deploy-apps-terminal-actions-api","reason":"The full pinned raw and SHA-256 verify the retained Management API action flow, API roles, ready upload IDs, maintenance/WebSocket timing, app closure, 100-ID limit, all-or-none ID validation versus later per-terminal scheduling errors, planned versus completed states, and the displayed curl path caveat. All five quote substrings and line locations check out. Both fixed answers preserve the scheduling and completion boundary. The central retrieval route is missing: this Android app/certificate deployment guide links only to the Terminal API payment-message concept, while the dedicated Android terminal hub already exists and explicitly owns app deployment routes."}
{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-point-of-sale-automating-terminal-management-configure-terminals-api","reason":"Full independent review verified the pinned raw SHA-256, five exact quotes and locations, and both fixed-query answers. The candidate accurately distinguishes Management API configuration from Terminal API payment messaging; preserves credential roles, sensitive settings, inheritance, GET/PATCH scope, omission and empty-value removal, logo model requirements, test examples, live rate limits, and device propagation. One central retrieval route is misplaced: the source has no link to the existing dedicated terminal-management hub, while its Overview and Related section point to POS store management and its sole reciprocal proposal would promote this configuration guide into a store-administration hub. A reader asking how to configure terminal features across company, merchant, store, or terminal levels could select the store-creation/payment-method route and miss the terminal-management task guide."}
{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-point-of-sale-standalone-standalone-build-set-up-standalone","reason":"The pinned 2026-09-15 raw matches the trusted SHA-256 and was fully read. The retained setup, timing, tipping, Quebec, refund-passcode, payment-facilitator, and test/live claims are supported; all five quotes and line locators match. The main retrieval route is misplaced: this guide is for direct standalone terminal initiation, but its Related section and only proposed reciprocal link route through the integrated Terminal API concept even though the dedicated standalone concept now exists. A query for how to enable direct terminal payments would therefore select the integrated API path as the main concept. The raw also gives a conditional Support contact for enabling tipping and referenced refunds, which should be kept visible with the configuration claim."}
